id: pm-rncuf7
title: "Annotation transposition recovery: detect pm <collection> add <id> before the item id is consumed as text"
description: "GitHub #979 reproduces a cross-collection agent grammar mistake: noun-verb-object input is parsed as id=add and text=<real item id>, then reported as a duplicate text-source collision. The refusal must recognize the resolvable item id, name the transposed subcommand, render role-labeled recovery data, and make the accepted --note alias discoverable or reject it. Duplicate check searched all statuses for notes add, transposed subcommand, annotation collision, item-id-as-text, and --note help; closed pm-185870 owns general unknown positional subcommands but not this annotation parser collision."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: agent-ux,annotations,"area:cli","area:sdk",contracts,error-recovery,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T22:24:03.100Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-11T22:24:02.510Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-11T22:24:02.510Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "When an annotation collection receives id=add and its text positional resolves to a real item, the typed SDK/CLI refusal names the transposed subcommand and supplies the canonical pm <collection> <id> --add form; the machine-readable recovery bundle labels parsed positional roles rather than flattening them; notes, learnings, files, docs, comments, and test share the behavior; the accepted --note alias is declared in help/contracts or removed with a typed migration refusal; focused unit, integration, packaged npm/npx/bun/bunx acceptance, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, and docstring gates pass"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Turn a common annotation grammar transposition into a one-turn, machine-actionable recovery"
value: Avoid repeated failed agent turns and prevent normalized recovery receipts from obscuring positional roles
impact: All annotation collections become safer and cheaper for agents to drive
why_now: "The defect reproduces on the latest immutable 2026.8.11 package and currently affects notes, learnings, files, docs, comments, and test workflows"
parent: pm-mpbb
reporter: GitHub #979
severity: medium
environment: "@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7, 2026.8.10, and 2026.8.11; Node 22/26; Linux"
repro_steps: "In a temporary workspace with item tst-y0bb, run pm notes add tst-y0bb --note hello; observe id=add/text=tst-y0bb collision guidance instead of transposed-subcommand recovery"
resolution: "Annotation transposition is recognized before mutation, recovery labels parser roles and supplies object-first syntax, --note is visible, and the generated error catalog is deterministically partitioned."
expected_result: "A typed refusal says add is not an annotation subcommand, identifies tst-y0bb as the item id, and shows pm notes tst-y0bb --add hello"
actual_result: The CLI reports that note text was supplied twice and emits a flat normalized_args receipt that hides which token filled each positional slot
