comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T18:12:18.364Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: all-status searches over annotation transposition, notes add, positional subcommand, item-id-as-text, collision, and alias help found closed pm-185870, pm-vcu7, pm-a2h3, pm-8nyc and open grammar owners pm-n7rr/pm-ya7x55. Their full live metadata confirms none owns the resolvable-id transposition diagnosis or hidden --note alias. Canonical external report: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/979."
  "2026-08-11T22:18:17.370Z","harness:codex","Evidence 2026-08-12: annotation noun-verb-object transposition now returns typed role-labelled recovery, notes visibly declares --note, and the generated error catalog is deterministically partitioned under repository line/directory limits. Exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, catalog freshness, surface replication, docstrings/static quality, packed dogfood, npx, and external-package smoke passed. Temporary acceptance confirmed pm notes --note succeeds and pm notes add <id> fails with annotation_transposed_subcommand plus parsed positional roles."
  "2026-08-11T22:23:34.343Z","harness:codex","Packed Bun acceptance 2026-08-12: npm pack produced unbrained-pm-cli-2026.8.11.tgz and bunx --silent --bun --package <tarball> pm --json --no-extensions contracts --summary exited 0 with schema_version 4.7.0 and 56 command summaries. Registry-backed package-default bunx remains assigned to the post-publish verifier, because Bun does not accept a tarball path in its package-default shorthand."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-11T22:18:17.978Z","harness:codex","Recovery payloads must preserve parser roles, not only normalized token order; generated public catalogs also need deterministic partitioning so strict source-size gates remain meaningful rather than waived."
